just this morning Apple released their  brand-new ear pods Pro that are priced  at 250 dollars and are already available  to order on their website so in this  video we're gonna tell you literally  everything you need to know about how  they work and how they compare to the  regular air pods first off the air pots  Pro come with the wireless charging case  so it's actually just fifty dollars more  than the air pods and from the looks of  it you truly get a lot for the extra  money they feature a brand new design  with a shorter stem and they come with  three sizes of silicone ear tips that  plug into your ears so they create a  seal for better deeper bass and will  have a better fit compared to regular  air pods which don't fit very well in  some people's ear canals the vents on  the outside of the air ponts Pro  equalize the pressure inside of your  ears so you'll never feel like your ears  are plugged like you do with some other  silicones have earphones they offer some  very cool features like active noise  cancellation and active EQ tuning which  I'll talk about in just a minute there's  also a new force sensor on the stem  which allows you to control off your  music by pressing on it instead of  tapping on it like before press wants to  play pause or answer a phone call press  twice to skip forward press three times  to skip backward and press and hold to  switch between noise cancellation mode  in transparent mode which basically uses  the microphones to listen to ambient  sound around you and play it directly  into your ears just like the live listen  feature and of course there's also hey  Siri support for volume and music  controls now one of the biggest  complaints of the regular air pods was  that they just didn't sound like a $200  pair of earphones and it seems like  Apple is finally fixing that the last  version of air pods were only able to  produce bass at a low frequency of  around 65 Hertz but this year's air pots  can go all the way down to 20 Hertz  which means seriously deep bass  reproduction the active noise  cancellation uses microphones to listen  to noise up to 200 times per second and  then the air Potts Pro send anti noise  signals to counter and eliminate it the  adaptive EQ feature uses microphones to  automatically tune the sound to the  shape of your ear so you get a wide  soundstage all the time no matter how  your ear canals are shaped the new  speaker drivers use the same technology  as Apple's home pod  to deliver distortion-free base and the  inward-facing microphone actually  listens for distortion and that adjusts  the frequencies to make sure there is  never any distortion Apple also boasted  about their new high dynamic range  amplifier so the sound quality should be  improved as well ear pods Pro also come  with the new h1 chip for reduced  Bluetooth lag improved power efficiency  support for hey Siri in a more stable  connection this allows for things like  streaming music to two separate pairs of  air pods from just one iphone that's  updated to iOS 13 the air pods Pro are  also ipx4 sweat and water-resistant just  like the power beats Pro and for the  battery life you get the same five hours  as the regular air pods if you're not  using the noise cancellation features  but if you are using them the battery  life only gets reduced by half an hour  which is really impressive not only that  but you actually get half an hour more  talk time during calls then the regular  air pots do and charging the air pods  Pro for just five minutes gets you an  extra hour of listening time now if you  include the charging case you actually  get over 24 hours of listening time just  like the regular air pods and the case  itself has actually gotten a little bit  bigger it's the same thickness as before  and it actually gotten a bit shorter but  it's quite a bit wider than before the  main thing is that it didn't get thicker  so it'll still feel very comfortable in  your pocket and once again I do want to  mention that it supports wireless  charging using any Qi compatible charger  now unfortunately the case still uses a  lightning port for charging but at least  it comes with the lightning to USB C  cable in the box for use with the new 18  watt USB C charger that comes with the  iPhone 11 pro now if you don't already  have a USB C power adapter I'll drop a  link down below on a very good deal on  an 18 watt USB C charger the air pods  Pro are already available to order right  now in Apple's website and we'll be  getting our pair delivered this Thursday  so if you want to see some in-depth  testing videos make sure to click that  subscribe button below so with all the  specs out of the way let me give my  personal thoughts on what matters about  the air Potts Pro and if they're  actually worth the extra fifty dollars  there were three main issues with the  original air pods  people didn't like the long-stem design  the unique shape didn't fit all ear  canals  so people who actually really wanted to  use earpods couldn't use them and  finally the sound quality wasn't as good  as other earphones in the same price  range it now seems like Apple has  attacked all three of these issues  shortening the stems making the fit  customizable with three sizes of  silicone tips and they seem like they've  worked on the sound quality as well  especially with the new adaptive EQ and  active noise cancellation features the  design itself has changed just enough  with the new stem design new black  styling on the outside in the new case  so you can easily tell the air pods Pro  from the regular air pots you're also  getting some added features like water  resistance and a much better control  system than before with a new force  sensor I personally think that the best  part about these earphones is that they  use the microphones to actively adjust  the frequency of sound as well as the  noise cancellation so that each user  gets high quality sound no matter how  their ears are shaped that's something  you can't get with any other earphones  right now so with all those added  features I think the extra 50 bucks is  definitely worth it for the air pods Pro  over the regular air pods and thanks to  the already great reputation of the  original air pods  especially for reliability people know  that the air Potts Pro are gonna work  great let us know your thoughts down in  the comments below and if you want to  see us unbox the air pods Pro on  Thursday and compare them to the  airport's to click that circle above to  subscribe thanks for watching and we'll  see you in the next video  [Music]
 

